// The language server's worker (0.24, docs/lsp.md): a copy of the server
// (fork) that reads the program once, with the open documents' unsaved
// texts in place of their files (OVERLAY), publishes its diagnostics,
// then answers the requests the server hands it from the tables the
// queries answer from: definition and references (the references every
// query collects, query/refs; locals, refactor_mod/local), hover (the
// signature `query def` prints, the effects and features, `query type`'s
// typed nodes), the document's symbols (`query items`' definitions), the
// workspace's symbols. The server replaces it when a document changes.
//
// (0.25) Every name resolves: std's items to std's text written as files
// (stdfiles.vl), an operator to the function it calls (`+`: Add::add), a
// type parameter to where it is declared; a hover on a keyword, an
// attribute or a primitive type explains it (words.vl), one on an item
// adds the comment above it. The references the checker records for what
// it made (a local's drop, an f-string's display, a contract's check) are
// not the program's: a name is what it is written as.
//
// Requests come one per line, `METHOD \t PATH \t LINE \t CHARACTER \t FLAG
// \t ID` (workspaceSymbol: the query in PATH); each answer goes back as a
// frame `KIND LENGTH\n` then the JSON message: `r` a response, `n` a
// notification (publishDiagnostics), `e` (empty) the end of the
// diagnostics; (0.25.2) `f` the program's files, one path a line, before
// them.

